-- Q7: Risk Assessment [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AU-C 315, the risk of material misstatement (RMM) comprises inherent risk and control risk. Inherent risk is the susceptibility of an assertion to misstatement before considering controls, and control risk is the risk that controls fail to prevent or detect such misstatements.
Wrong (A): Audit risk is the overall model (RMM multiplied by detection risk), not a component of RMM. Detection risk is the auditor''s component.
Wrong (C): Sampling risk and nonsampling risk relate to the auditor''s procedures, not the entity''s risk of misstatement.
Wrong (D): Business risk and information risk are general concepts, not components of the audit risk model under GAAS.$EXPL$
